                <pb facs="0646" n="606" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v05/pg606"/>

                <head>203. Memorandum of a Conversation Between President Frondizi and the Chargé in Argentina (Beaulac), Buenos Aires, November 5, 1959<anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d203-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Buenos Aires</placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" type="conversation-or-meeting-date"
                            when="1959-11-05">November 5, 1959</date></dateline></opener>
                <list subtype="subject" type="description">
                    <label>SUBJECT</label>
                    <item>Military Credits</item>
                </list>
                <p>The President stated that he had just heard from Ambassador Del Carril regarding
                    our inability to deviate from the usual three-year credit terms on the sale of
                    military equipment desired by Argentina. He stated that he was disappointed but
                    that since the equipment was so greatly needed by the Argentine Armed Forces,
                    instructions were being promptly sent to the Embassy in Washington to accept
                    these terms.</p>
                <p>I explained to him again the circumstances surrounding credits for military
                    equipment which had made it impossible to work out any more liberal terms, as
                    had originally been hoped by the Latin American Division of the Department. He
                    said he understood and would go ahead.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d203-f2"/></p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d203-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d203-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Department of State, Central Files, 735.56/11–959. Confidential.
                    Transmitted in despatch 730 from Buenos Aires, November 9.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d203-f2" n="2" xml:id="d203-f2-content">
                <p>On November 19, the National Advisory Council advised the Departments of State
                    and Defense that it offered no objection to their consideration of a credit of
                    $11.1 million to Argentina to assist in financing the sale of military equipment
                    and services totaling $12.35 million under the terms of the Mutual Security Act
                    of 1954, as amended. The credit was to be repaid in U.S. dollars in semiannual
                    or annual installments over a 3-year period with interest at the rate of 3½
                    percent per year. (Memorandum from Bell
                    to Irwin, November 27; <hi
                        rendition="#italic">ibid</hi>., 735.56/11–2759)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
